    <dt>Agenda version</dt><dd>Draft v. 21 Oct 2026</dd>
   </dl>
   <div class="note" style="margin-bottom:0">Per the organizer’s agenda, panelists give framing talks of 7 minutes (max 10); speakers should plan <b>3 slides maximum</b>. Most of each panel is moderated discussion.</div>
  </div>
  <div class="card">
   <h3 style="margin-top:0">Meeting purpose</h3>
   <p>The working group focuses on translating microbiome research into clinically actionable cancer-care recommendations — identifying consensus and evidence gaps, defining research priorities, developing standards for clinical and translational evidence, and informing future practice.</p>
   <p>Meeting 1 focused on establishing what is known. Meeting 2 focuses on establishing what is needed to bring the microbiome to clinical care: consensus statements on what is clinically actionable today, a research agenda, and evidence standards for the manuscript to be submitted to <i>Nature Medicine</i> on March 15, 2027. All members will have the opportunity to review the manuscript and sign off on authorship.</p>
  </div>
